---
// The article text (.cl-source) goes in the slot, inside the original's
// column, in both column layouts. Switching between 1段 and n段 changes the
// styles around it but never moves it: a moved element loses its styles and
// boxes, and laying the whole article out from scratch was most of the
// switch's time (docs/column-layout.md, "操作への応答"). In 1段 the wrappers
// are plain blocks in the article; the reader adds cl-track and cl-slot to
// them in n段, and Layout.astro does when it opens an article in n段.
//
// The original's column (.cl-original) is the plane's first child, and the
// copies' columns go at the end of .cl-copies, which has no box. Adding a copy
// as a sibling of the original's column restyled the whole original text in
// the reader's first frame: in Firefox when the original's column stopped
// being the last child, in Chromium when the copy went before a later sibling.
---
<div class="cl-reader">
  <div class="cl-viewport">
    <div class="cl-plane"><div class="cl-original"><div class="cl-original-slot"><slot /><div class="cl-paper" aria-hidden="true"></div></div></div><div class="cl-copies"></div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="cl-ruler" aria-hidden="true"><div></div></div>

<script>
  import { initializeColumnLayout } from "../scripts/column-layout";
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", initializeColumnLayout);
</script>
